## 4. Permissions and requests

Want to use BrowserX commercially, modify it, or publish something based on it?
Ask. Requests go to the Author through the project's GitHub page or the website
above. Written permission may be granted (with conditions, if appropriate);
without written permission the answer is no.

---

## 5. Third-party components (not covered by this licence)

BrowserX builds on other people's work, and that work keeps its own licence. This
licence applies **only** to the original code written for BrowserX:

| Component | Licence |
|---|---|
| [Chromium](https://www.chromium.org/) — the engine (Blink, V8, network stack) | BSD-3-Clause plus third-party licences |
| [CEF — Chromium Embedded Framework](https://github.com/chromiumembedded/cef) | BSD-3-Clause |
| Android platform and NDK interface headers (mobile edition) | Apache-2.0 |
| CEF headers vendored in `.cef-headers/` (used for offline compile checks) | CEF's own BSD-3-Clause, notices left intact |

Two consequences, stated plainly:

* Nothing in this licence takes away a right that a third-party licence gives
  you, and nothing in those licences gives you rights to BrowserX's original
  code. See [CREDITS.md](CREDITS.md).
* The **bundled Chromium/CEF runtime** that `make deps` downloads and
  `make package` ships is that third-party software, under its own licences.
  BrowserX claims no copyright over it.

